        "math_academy_id": "q-334484",
        "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ compute $P(-0.92<Z<-0.18).$ Use the tables below and do not round your answer.\n\n| | $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1841\\,$ | $\\,0.1814\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2119\\,$ | $\\,0.2090\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ | |  | | $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.4721\\,$ | $\\,0.4681\\,$ | $\\,0.4641\\,$ | |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.0\\,$ | $\\,0.1587\\,$ | $\\,0.1562\\,$ | $\\,0.1539\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.9\\,$ | $\\,0.1841\\,$ | $\\,0.1814\\,$ | $\\,0.1788\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.2119\\,$ | $\\,0.2090\\,$ | $\\,0.2061\\,$ |\n| $z$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ | $\\,0.08\\,$ | $\\,0.09\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.2\\,$ | $\\,0.3936\\,$ | $\\,0.3897\\,$ | $\\,0.3859\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.1\\,$ | $\\,0.4325\\,$ | $\\,0.4286\\,$ | $\\,0.4247\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.0\\,$ | $\\,0.4721\\,$ | $\\,0.4681\\,$ | $\\,0.4641\\,$ |\n\n$P(-0.92<Z<-0.18)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        "worked_solution": "We're given that $Z\u223cN(0,1),$ and we wish to compute $P(-0.92<Z<-0.18).$ The required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069404/assets/34132169270b3259fb1be909f7aea2474e4dff1375603e9b9a75e013900f6340.png)\n\nBy the definition of the cumulative distribution function $\u03a6(z),$ \n\n$$\nP(Z\\le z)=\u03a6(z).\n$$\n\nSo, we express the required probability in terms of $\u03a6(z)$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.92<Z<-0.18) & =P(Z<-0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.92) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le -0.18)-P(Z\\le -0.92) \\\\  & =\u03a6(-0.18)-\u03a6(-0.92).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the tables, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03a6(-0.92) & =0.1788 \\\\ \u03a6(-0.18) & =0.4286\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(-0.92<Z<-0.18) & =\u03a6(-0.18)-\u03a6(-0.92) \\\\  & =0.4286-0.1788 \\\\  & =0.2498.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
